# Chevra Ahavas Chesed

Read `AGENTS.md` before editing data, the web map, or the PDF.

## Sources

Leave these bytes unchanged: `cemetery map.png`, `master list of departed poorly formatted.pdf`, `list of departed since 2020 (11-10-26).pdf`.

## Order of work

1. `data/burials.csv` and `data/qa-issues.csv`
2. Confirm the open questions in `AGENTS.md`, then `data/plots.csv`
3. Static map in `web/`
4. Indexed PDF in `print/`

## Grid

- Single-letter fields: 18 lots per row. Double- and triple-letter fields: 14.
- Working row count is 3. Ask before adding a row.
- Fields in the master list: A–S, AA–JJ, AAA–KKK.
- Fields J–O use lot numbers above 18. Keep the printed lot and record a QA issue. Leave those lots unrenumbered.
- KK and LLL appear only in later records. Ask before drawing them.
- Lot status is `occupied`, `empty`, or `reserved`. Use `reserved` only when Stanley or the cemetery named that lot.

## Records

Keep the printed name, date, and location in raw columns. Master names are last-then-first. Recent names are first-then-last. Rosedale and buried-elsewhere rows stay in the CSV and stay off the Chevra grave map.

## Find a Grave

There is no public read API suitable for this project. Do not scrape the site and do not call its undocumented endpoint.

## Example

Master: `Baer Adolph R 3 17 9/6/20`
Recent: `Adolph (Eddie) Baer 9/6/20 Field R, Row 3, Lot 17`
Those are one person. Store both source lines on one CSV row when field, row, lot, and date agree.
